# Stage 11 — Git LFS for binary AI-generated assets.
#
# Contract: assets <=1MB stay on plain git for clonability without LFS;
# assets >1MB go through LFS. Audio + video always go to LFS regardless
# of size (they're rarely tiny and they add up fast).
#
# Sidecars (*.json) ALWAYS stay on plain git — they're tiny, must be
# diff-readable, and are the audit trail. See
# .agent_governance/rules/asset-generation.md.
#
# NOTE: Git LFS does not gate by file size natively. PNG over 1MB is
# handled by convention: when the wrapper writes one, the operator
# runs `git lfs track "<path>"` for that specific asset (which appends
# an entry below). Audio/video are tracked unconditionally.

*.ogg  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.wav  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.mp3  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.webm filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.mp4  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.mov  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Sidecars stay text/diffable.
*.json -filter -diff -merge text

# Conventional bitmap polish directories: PNGs over 1MB will be
# tracked explicitly via `git lfs track "art/bitmap/large/<file>.png"`
# at the time they land. Small PNGs (the typical sprite case) stay on
# plain git so the repo remains clonable without LFS.
